AP Reelume (the "Program") is owned by Carlos Armando Puche Martín, trading as
AP Smart Code Solutions (the "Owner"). This licence describes what you may and
may not do with it. Its full text travels with the Program, in the LICENSE file,
and is published next to each download. The Program shows it in full before it
is first used, and can only be used after it is accepted with «I accept»; if you
do not agree with it, do not accept it and do not use the Program. What the law
allows you to do without the Owner's authorisation does not
depend on this licence.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

The Owner grants you a free of charge, worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable right, for an indefinite term, to:

  1.1 Install and use the Program on as many devices as you wish, at no cost and
      with no time limit.
  1.2 Use it for any purpose, personal or professional, including the commercial
      activity of the person using it.
  1.3 Make the backup copies of the installer and of the installed Program that
      you need in order to use it.
  1.4 Read the source code of the third-party components the Program
      incorporates, wherever it is published, under the terms of their own
      licences, and check with the signed checksums that accompany each release
      that the program you download is the one the Owner published.

There is nothing to pay, no registration and no account.

The Owner may end this right only as set out in clause 9. The Owner may stop
distributing or updating the Program at any time, and that does not take away
your right to keep using the copy you already have.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Except where applicable law expressly permits it notwithstanding this licence,
you may not:

  2.1 Modify the Program, its source code or its binaries, or create derivative
      works of it.
  2.2 Redistribute it: publish, share, host, package or hand it to third
      parties, whether free of charge or for a fee, in whole or in part.
  2.3 Sell, rent, assign, lend or sublicense it, or offer it as a service.
  2.4 Decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer it, except as this licence
      allows and as the law does not let a contract exclude: observing, studying
      and testing how it works (article 100.3 of the Spanish Intellectual
      Property Act) and decompiling it for interoperability under the
      conditions of paragraphs 5 and 6 of that article.
  2.5 Remove or alter copyright, licence or attribution notices, or the marks.
  2.6 Use the names "AP Reelume" or "AP Smart Code Solutions", or their logos,
      to identify or promote any other product or service.

This licence grants you no right over the names "AP Reelume" or "AP Smart Code
Solutions", nor over their logos or distinctive signs, other than to mention
them in order to identify the Program truthfully.

As an exception to 2.1, 2.4 and clause 3, and because section 6 of the GNU
Lesser General Public License 2.1 requires it, you are permitted to modify the
Program for your own use and to reverse engineer it for debugging such
modifications. This exception does not entitle you to distribute the modified
Program and does not extend to the NVIDIA components in clause 4 bis.

3. OWNERSHIP

The Program is licensed, not sold. The Owner retains ownership and all
intellectual property rights in it, including those this licence does not
expressly mention. Beyond what this licence and the law allow you, only the
Owner may modify the Program, and only the Owner decides whether it is
commercialised and on what terms.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Program incorporates third-party components governed by their own licences,
which prevail over this one in everything concerning those components, except
NVIDIA's, governed by clause 4 bis. The inventory of those components, the
licence of each and the full text of each licence travel inside the package, in
the `licenses/` folder, and are listed in the NOTICE file.

Nothing in this licence limits, or is intended to limit, the rights those
third-party licences grant you over those components.

4 bis. NVIDIA COMPONENTS

Some versions of the Program include NVIDIA Corporation components that enhance
the picture: the super-resolution engine and the part that connects it to the
Program. They belong to NVIDIA and its suppliers, who keep all their rights.
NVIDIA grants you no licence: you use them only through this one, and on these
terms:

  a) Only as part of the Program, on a computer with an NVIDIA graphics card.
  b) You may not extract them, copy them separately, distribute them, modify
     them or create derivative works of them.
  c) You may not decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer them, except to the
     extent mandatory law allows. Nor may you remove their notices or bypass
     their technical or security limits.
  d) The LGPL exception in clause 2 does not apply to them, nor does any term
     that would subject them to an open-source licence.
  e) You may not use them in systems whose failure could cause injury, death or
     catastrophic loss, such as aviation, navigation, military use, medicine or
     life support.
  f) You must comply with United States export-control and sanctions rules and
     any others that apply. You declare that you do not reside in a country or
     region under United States embargo and that you are not barred from
     receiving them.
  g) To the maximum extent the law allows, NVIDIA gives no warranty on them and
     has no liability to you. Their presence does not mean that NVIDIA sponsors
     or endorses the Program.
  h) If you breach this clause, your right to use the NVIDIA components ends
     immediately, without the cure period in clause 9.

5. THE SOURCE CODE AND CONTRIBUTIONS

The Program's source code is not published. What the Owner publishes in a public
repository hosted by a third party is the licence notices, the source code of
the third-party components their licences require, and the releases of the
Program for download. None of that grants you any right over the Program beyond
those of this licence, and everything set out in clause 2 remains prohibited.

Should you come to know the Program's source code by any means, that does not
entitle you to copy it, reuse it or incorporate it into any other work.

The Owner does not accept third-party code contributions and will reject those
